The cross product of vectors $\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ -2 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix}$ and $\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 3 \\ 6 \end{pmatrix}$ is calculated as:
\[
\begin{pmatrix} 
(-2)(6) - (5)(3) \\ 
(5)(-1) - (6)(4) \\ 
(4)(3) - (-2)(-1) 
\end{pmatrix} 
= \begin{pmatrix} 
-12 - 15 \\ 
-5 - 24 \\ 
12 - 2 
\end{pmatrix} 
= \begin{pmatrix} 
-27 \\ 
-29 \\ 
10 
\end{pmatrix}
\]
Thus, the cross product is $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -27 \\ -29 \\ 10 \end{pmatrix}}$.

